    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">15 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip ok\">Easy</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Trees</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Bottom-up DFS</span><span class=\"chip\">BFS</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-depth-of-binary-tree/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 104</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Maximum Depth of Binary Tree</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: a tree's depth is one more than the deeper of its two subtrees, and an empty tree has depth 0; a post-order DFS (or a level-by-level BFS that counts levels) answers it. O(n) time, O(h) stack.</p>\n"
